{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T08:51:57.953Z","ordinal":4664,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0be3b8594dbded3e016a9540a645cc87d1a6f98d2758cdbdea","status":"completed","call_id":"call_oBiPh4hDu6CXKFqspwiZ8jkQ","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/cd3-cta-final-20260831/CD3_CTA_OPTIMIZATION_REPORT.md\\n+# CD3 N64/N128 CTA optimization\\n+\\n+Date: 2026-08-31  \\n+GPU: NVIDIA GH200 480GB  \\n+Weights: real Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct layer 40, TP=1  \\n+Timing: warmup 10, iterations 100, L2 flush on, concurrent H2D on, P50\\n+\\n+## Retained implementation\\n+\\n+- N64 keeps the three-stage B/sign-mantissa pipeline but stores code bytes in\\n+  a two-entry ring. Code is consumed before WGMMA, so the old entry is safely\\n+  reused without shortening the compute pipeline.\\n+- N128 keeps three compressed-data stages and uses a two-entry B ring. The next\\n+  B entry is refilled only after the WGMMA using that buffer completes.\\n+- Final split-K policy:\\n+  - N<=64: QKV/O/GateUp/Down = 4\\n+  - N=128: QKV/O/Down = 4, GateUp = 1\\n+\\n+## Resource validation\\n+\\n+| kernel | registers/thread | dynamic shared/block | block limit | theoretical occupancy | achieved occupancy |\\n+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| N64 baseline | 80 | 46.85 KiB | 4 | 25.00% | 21.40% |\\n+| N64 final | 80 | 45.31 KiB | 5 | 31.25% | 24.71% |\\n+| N128 baseline | 124 | about 69.8 KiB | 3 | 18.75% | - |\\n+| N128 final mixed | 124 | 55.04 KiB | 4 | 25.00% | 22.95% |\\n+\\n+All retained kernels have zero local stack allocation.\\n+\\n+## Three-run mean fused-H2D milliseconds\\n+\\n+| N | version | QKV | O | GateUp | Down | sum |\\n+|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| 64 | baseline | 0.142373 | 0.096880 | 0.555520 | 0.288709 | 1.083483 |\\n+| 64 | final | 0.113781 | 0.097040 | 0.533301 | 0.289189 | 1.033312 |\\n+| 128 | baseline | 0.158875 | 0.135659 | 0.702315 | 0.410608 | 1.407456 |\\n+| 128 | final | 0.150011 | 0.109691 | 0.619296 | 0.330219 | 1.209216 |\\n+\\n+- N64 improves 4.6% over the immediately preceding CD3 version.\\n+- N128 improves 14.1% over the immediately preceding CD3 version.\\n+\\n+## Final same-process P4Flat comparison\\n+\\n+| N | P4Flat fused sum | CD3 fused sum | result |\\n+|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| 64 | 1.084176 | 1.035168 | CD3 4.5% faster |\\n+| 128 | 1.668000 | 1.212992 | CD3 27.3% faster |\\n+\\n+At N128, selecting the faster of P4Flat fused and decomp+GEMM independently\\n+for each projection gives 1.419872 ms; final CD3 is still 14.6% faster.\\n+\\n+## Rejected candidate\\n+\\n+Changing the entire N128 pipeline from three stages to two did reach four\\n+CTAs/SM, but regressed the three-run sum from 1.407456 to 1.513701 ms (7.6%).\\n+The retained mixed pipeline avoids that decode-prefetch loss.\\n+\\n+## Validation\\n+\\n+- `tests/test_chunk_delta3.py`: 13 passed.\\n+- All benchmark fused correctness checks passed.\\n+- Patch: `CD3_N64_5CTA_N128_4CTA.patch`\\n*** End Patch\";\nconst r = await tools.apply_patch(patch);\ntext(r);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a056f9-b66e-7300-898d-7d4e65cdc665","create_time":1788166309.124689}}}
